1
00:00:01,054 --> 00:00:03,060
The Wrath of the Great Earth

2
00:00:04,855 --> 00:00:06,421
Did you make a wish?

3
00:00:06,421 --> 00:00:07,392
What do you mean?

4
00:00:07,392 --> 00:00:13,095
The people of this planet believe that if we make a wish upon a shooting star, it will come true. What would you wish for?

5
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:17,013
Maybe I’d wish for all of the Wild Cardbots to be able to live peacefully on this planet.

6
00:00:17,013 --> 00:00:18,429
What would you wish for?

7
00:00:18,429 --> 00:00:22,888
Me? I'd wish... What would I wish for?

8
00:00:24,096 --> 00:00:26,251
Oh. Speaking of which...

9
00:00:26,251 --> 00:00:27,986
No. That's...

10
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,507
That's not a shooting star!

11
00:00:31,721 --> 00:00:32,582
Hm?

12
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:39,878
WAAAAGH!!

13
00:00:39,878 --> 00:00:42,152
Roar?! What was that?! An enemy ambush?!

14
00:00:42,152 --> 00:00:45,503
Given the force of the impact, it must've occurred not too far from here.

15
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:46,442
Jun!

16
00:00:47,472 --> 00:00:49,070
Something fell from the sky.

17
00:00:49,658 --> 00:00:50,506
Let's go!

18
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:52,979
Be careful down there.

19
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:54,326
Sir. Thank you for your service at this hour!

20
00:00:54,987 --> 00:00:55,649
Soleil!

21
00:00:55,649 --> 00:00:56,463
Jun!

22
00:00:57,305 --> 00:00:59,490
Is that what I think it is?

23
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:02,890
Yes. It must be an escape pod from planet Machina.

24
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:04,198
That escape pod looks like...!

25
00:01:04,198 --> 00:01:05,992
I wonder who's in there...

26
00:01:05,992 --> 00:01:07,917
I think that may be the passenger.

27
00:01:08,763 --> 00:01:12,998
So, this is the Metal Cardbot who was inside the escape pod?

28
00:01:12,998 --> 00:01:14,930
You sure it isn't just a regular excavator?

29
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:17,753
Yes. But no matter how many times I call out to them, they won’t respond.

30
00:01:17,753 --> 00:01:20,212
Do you think they were damaged by the impact of the landing?

31
00:01:20,212 --> 00:01:21,849
They'll wake up after I pick a fight with 'em!

32
00:01:21,849 --> 00:01:22,754
Mind if I join in?

33
00:01:22,754 --> 00:01:23,263
Eh?

34
00:01:23,263 --> 00:01:25,335
This is no time for jokes.

35
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:27,986
Uncle Edd, you’re not doing a half-hearted job back there, are you?

36
00:01:27,986 --> 00:01:29,885
I'm doing everything I can, thank you very much!

37
00:01:29,885 --> 00:01:32,506
Why not just seal them now, regardless of whether they wake up or not?

38
00:01:32,506 --> 00:01:38,247
Soleil... How would you feel if somebody locked you up inside a cramped room while you were asleep, without your permission?

39
00:01:38,247 --> 00:01:39,977
I'd... close my heart to them.

40
00:01:39,977 --> 00:01:40,875
Right?

41
00:01:40,875 --> 00:01:43,146
Jun, how about you scan them with your Metal Breath?

42
00:01:43,146 --> 00:01:45,274
Ah! I forgot I could do that.

43
00:01:46,227 --> 00:01:47,859
(Hm. This gives me deja vu...)

44
00:01:47,859 --> 00:01:51,109
[Data Retrieval Complete. Wild Cardbot. Codename: Solid Horn.]

45
00:01:51,109 --> 00:01:51,606
What?!

46
00:01:51,606 --> 00:01:52,576
Did it say Solid Horn?!

47
00:01:52,576 --> 00:01:53,746
You mean this guy?!

48
00:01:53,746 --> 00:01:54,820
Do you know who he is?

49
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:58,134
He is the chieftain of the Monohorn tribe, which ruled the forested region of planet Machina.

50
00:01:58,134 --> 00:01:59,204
He's a chieftain?

51
00:01:59,204 --> 00:02:05,082
How strange. The way I know him, he’s the sort who pierces rocks with his horn and shakes the earth with his hammer.

52
00:02:05,082 --> 00:02:06,862
Yet, he looks rather small for that.

53
00:02:06,862 --> 00:02:08,235
What, he doesn't look the same or something?

54
00:02:08,235 --> 00:02:10,223
But the scan says it's him.

55
00:02:10,223 --> 00:02:12,888
There's no way there would be an error in the Metal Breath's data.

56
00:02:12,888 --> 00:02:14,413
Solid Horn...

57
00:02:14,413 --> 00:02:20,139
He was a fearsome Wild Cardbot warrior who single-handedly pushed an entire squad of Star Guardians to the very brink of annihilation.

58
00:02:20,139 --> 00:02:22,334
I was part of that squad as well.

59
00:02:24,579 --> 00:02:29,806
However, his rampage was barely halted thanks to Flame Nova, who was my superior at the time...

60
00:02:29,806 --> 00:02:31,278
Flame Nova stopped him?

61
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:41,427
...and eventually, he was arrested and sealed away in the prison known as "Trion".

62
00:02:41,627 --> 00:02:43,507
Are we really sure this is the same guy?

63
00:02:43,507 --> 00:02:46,325
This situation feels kind of familiar...

64
00:02:46,325 --> 00:02:48,010
[Inspector, a vehicle is approaching.]

65
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,625
Copy that. Let it through.

66
00:02:49,625 --> 00:02:50,281
Crest!

67
00:02:50,281 --> 00:02:52,858
I had a feeling that everyone would be gathered here. Hello, inspector.

68
00:02:52,858 --> 00:02:53,694
Big brother.

69
00:02:53,694 --> 00:02:54,718
Soleil.

70
00:02:54,718 --> 00:02:55,944
What did you bring with you?

71
00:02:55,944 --> 00:02:56,651
Ah, that's-

72
00:02:56,651 --> 00:02:59,865
We'll tell you later. We came here because of the meteor that fell around here last night.

73
00:03:00,401 --> 00:03:02,313
A total of three meteors fell.

74
00:03:02,313 --> 00:03:03,306
Three?

75
00:03:03,306 --> 00:03:06,484
I, too, clearly saw the meteor split into three pieces as it was falling.

76
00:03:06,484 --> 00:03:11,318
And it looks like one of those meteors fell 25 kilometers west of Mowtown.

77
00:03:11,318 --> 00:03:15,412
I was informed that it was a meteorite, but I guess it must've been another escape pod.

78
00:03:15,412 --> 00:03:17,114
Yes. That's highly likely.

79
00:03:17,114 --> 00:03:20,121
The first escape pod we found is the same kind of pod that Heavy Iron had arrived in.

80
00:03:20,121 --> 00:03:22,109
Oh! I knew this all felt familiar!

81
00:03:22,109 --> 00:03:23,930
Heavy Iron? That semi-trailer truck?

82
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:27,319
When he came to Earth in that escape pod, it had split into several separate pods, just like this one did.

83
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:30,030
Yeah. His body was also split into two for some reason.

84
00:03:30,030 --> 00:03:35,007
He was all like "Oooooh, gimme back by bodyyyyy~!" And then he chased us and took his body back.

85
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:37,191
Uh... Wait! Could this be...?

86
00:03:37,191 --> 00:03:39,771
We need to check the escape pod first. Let's hurry!

87
00:03:39,771 --> 00:03:40,497
Right!

88
00:03:43,138 --> 00:03:44,356
Inspector Holden!

89
00:03:44,356 --> 00:03:45,211
Is this it?

90
00:03:45,211 --> 00:03:50,487
Yes, sir. We received a report that campers witnessed a meteor fall into the lake last night, so we went to retrieve it...

91
00:03:51,213 --> 00:03:53,718
Yep. This is the same kind of escape pod!

92
00:03:53,718 --> 00:03:55,352
Let's hurry and check inside.

93
00:03:57,352 --> 00:03:59,662
It looks different from the first one that fell.

94
00:03:59,662 --> 00:04:03,205
[Data Retrieval Complete. Wild Cardbot. Codename: Solid Horn.]

95
00:04:03,205 --> 00:04:04,110
Knew it.

96
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:06,132
How is this possible? It has the same ID.

97
00:04:06,132 --> 00:04:09,264
Hey. Who are you? Are you truly Solid Horn?

98
00:04:09,264 --> 00:04:11,259
Looks like this guy is also exercising his right to remain silent.

99
00:04:11,259 --> 00:04:11,787
Jun.

100
00:04:11,787 --> 00:04:12,500
Hm?

101
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:18,291
Just like Heavy Iron, Flame Nova was also split into four parts and sealed away because he angered Deus Machina.

102
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:20,483
If Solid Horn is the same case as them...

103
00:04:20,483 --> 00:04:23,838
Those three meteors... are Solid Horn's seperated body parts?

104
00:04:23,838 --> 00:04:27,004
If that's the case, then where is the main unit?

105
00:04:27,891 --> 00:04:28,680
What's that sound?

106
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,831
It sounds like... a drumbeat?

107
00:04:30,831 --> 00:04:32,329
Oh-ho. This beat...

108
00:04:32,329 --> 00:04:34,870
My blood boils whenever I hear it!

109
00:04:34,870 --> 00:04:36,816
What's going on with you guys all of a sudden?

110
00:04:37,754 --> 00:04:38,752
Hm?

111
00:04:38,752 --> 00:04:41,350
Who the heck is banging on a drum at this hour?

112
00:04:41,350 --> 00:04:42,341
AGH!!

113
00:04:47,441 --> 00:04:49,009
What exactly is this drumbeat?

114
00:04:49,009 --> 00:04:51,411
It's the battle drumbeat passed down through the Monohorn tribe.

115
00:04:51,411 --> 00:04:52,283
What??

116
00:04:52,283 --> 00:04:53,543
Hey, Uncle Edd.

117
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:57,952
Jun! I heard a strange drumbeat, and then the excavator suddenly bolted out of the garage on its own!

118
00:04:57,952 --> 00:04:59,546
So he woke up...

119
00:05:04,812 --> 00:05:06,187
It's starting to move!

120
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:07,968
Grab it!

121
00:05:07,968 --> 00:05:09,887
Where do you think you're going?!

122
00:05:10,088 --> 00:05:11,326
Look over there!

123
00:05:11,326 --> 00:05:12,067
Not another one!

124
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:14,752
It looks like his body parts are gathering here...!

125
00:05:14,752 --> 00:05:17,192
Inspector Holden! Please evacuate everyone from the area!

126
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:20,302
Copy that! Everyone! Let's get outta here!

127
00:05:20,302 --> 00:05:21,112
You guys too!

128
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:24,567
We have some trusty friends here, so we'll be fine! Go ahead without us!

129
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,523
Alright. Be careful out there!

130
00:05:26,523 --> 00:05:28,033
Tigun! Take care of the excavator!

131
00:05:28,033 --> 00:05:31,043
GRRR!! I've been waiting for you to summon me!

132
00:05:31,043 --> 00:05:32,658
Phantom Hornet! Aid Tigun!

133
00:05:32,658 --> 00:05:34,528
Bzzt! Leave it to me!

134
00:05:40,237 --> 00:05:40,941
Dang!

135
00:05:40,941 --> 00:05:41,913
After him!

136
00:05:46,783 --> 00:05:47,483
That jerk!

137
00:05:47,483 --> 00:05:48,971
May I join in as well?

138
00:05:48,971 --> 00:05:51,177
Yeah! Please take care of the crane truck.

139
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:54,887
Hmph... Gathered at last.

140
00:05:54,887 --> 00:05:57,384
Living in this wretched form is finally over!

141
00:05:58,406 --> 00:05:59,435
Is that...

142
00:05:59,435 --> 00:06:01,038
...Solid Horn's main unit?

143
00:06:01,771 --> 00:06:03,601
We can't let them gather in the same spot!

144
00:06:13,483 --> 00:06:15,137
Star Guardian...!

145
00:06:15,137 --> 00:06:18,740
Well, well. I had no idea there'd be so many guests here already!

146
00:06:19,418 --> 00:06:20,266
Hm?

147
00:06:20,266 --> 00:06:21,516
CAAAWWWW!!!

148
00:06:21,516 --> 00:06:22,338
Bzzt!

149
00:06:22,444 --> 00:06:23,307
Growl!

150
00:06:23,307 --> 00:06:24,130
Look out!

151
00:06:31,413 --> 00:06:34,817
I guess I've been wandering the universe for far too long...

152
00:06:35,406 --> 00:06:38,336
But who cares? I've got freedom in my grasp now!

153
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:44,639
Here in this new land, I can run wild to my heart's content!

154
00:06:45,975 --> 00:06:47,913
That's... his complete form?

155
00:06:47,913 --> 00:06:48,704
This is bad...

156
00:06:48,704 --> 00:06:52,956
Grrhaha! Look! The mighty chieftain has regained his precious body!

157
00:06:56,694 --> 00:06:57,165
Soleil!

158
00:06:57,165 --> 00:06:57,634
Mhm.

159
00:06:58,444 --> 00:06:58,932
Tigun!

160
00:06:58,932 --> 00:06:59,858
Phantom Hornet!

161
00:06:59,858 --> 00:07:00,702
Set Up!

162
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:07,690
This isn’t the great forest on Planet Machina where you used to run wild! We don’t have to fight the Metal Cardbots anymore!

163
00:07:07,690 --> 00:07:12,038
Tch... To hear such feeble words from my own kind... You’ve really become a bunch of wimps!

164
00:07:12,437 --> 00:07:17,060
We’re still beasts, but this new life here ain’t so bad either!

165
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:20,903
We realized that after spending time with the guys here!

166
00:07:20,903 --> 00:07:25,668
The guys here, you say... You mean those tiny fleshlings and that disgraceful Star Guardian?!

167
00:07:25,668 --> 00:07:27,456
Night Griffon! Set Up!

168
00:07:32,004 --> 00:07:34,476
I fully understand that you want to let your spirit run wild...

169
00:07:34,476 --> 00:07:36,197
Scream Of Talon!

170
00:07:36,197 --> 00:07:38,158
...but the game has changed!

171
00:07:41,401 --> 00:07:44,269
I feel a bit powerless. Guess I haven't fully woken up yet...

172
00:07:44,269 --> 00:07:47,314
Time to awaken that wild power I've been longing for!

173
00:07:52,553 --> 00:07:53,509
CAAAAW!!

174
00:07:53,509 --> 00:07:54,711
Night Griffon!!

175
00:07:55,908 --> 00:07:57,139
Tigun! Set Up!

176
00:08:02,962 --> 00:08:03,987
Be careful!

177
00:08:11,326 --> 00:08:12,242
Guys!!

178
00:08:12,704 --> 00:08:16,613
Oh dear... Is this the karmic retribution for my past actions? Cough...

179
00:08:16,613 --> 00:08:20,730
Grrr! Is that all you got? Bring me another!

180
00:08:21,127 --> 00:08:22,668
Soleil. I'll fight him.

181
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,216
You can't fight him alone! Jun!

182
00:08:24,216 --> 00:08:25,572
Mhm! Blue Cop!

183
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:26,334
Yes!

184
00:08:26,533 --> 00:08:27,161
Blue Cop!

185
00:08:27,161 --> 00:08:28,000
Blaion!

186
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:28,646
Set Up!

187
00:08:31,442 --> 00:08:33,107
Blue Cop! Open fire!

188
00:08:35,769 --> 00:08:37,457
Blaion, aim for his legs!

189
00:08:45,818 --> 00:08:51,240
A Wild Cardbot being obedient to those little fleshlings and a Star Guardian?! I can't believe it!

190
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:55,315
Earth is not planet Machina! That distinction doesn't matter anymore!

191
00:08:55,715 --> 00:08:59,192
If the Wild Cardbots can live in peace in this new land,

192
00:08:59,192 --> 00:09:02,071
I'll do whatever it takes... no matter how tough the path may be!

193
00:09:02,071 --> 00:09:04,970
Muhaha. Take your "peace" and shove it!

194
00:09:07,086 --> 00:09:09,126
Wild Guardy! Guardian Shield!!

195
00:09:12,543 --> 00:09:13,423
Not bad.

196
00:09:13,423 --> 00:09:14,511
Wild Guardy, that's...

197
00:09:14,511 --> 00:09:17,697
Buster Gallon made this shield based on my Weapon Card.

198
00:09:17,697 --> 00:09:20,282
It's not as good as the original, but you can leave the defensive work to me!

199
00:09:20,282 --> 00:09:21,687
I've been wondering what that was.

200
00:09:21,687 --> 00:09:24,375
Big brother, how did you do that when you don't have a Metal Breath...?

201
00:09:24,375 --> 00:09:26,114
We don't need anything like that.

202
00:09:26,114 --> 00:09:27,553
Because we're connected by our hearts.

203
00:09:27,553 --> 00:09:28,767
By your... hearts...?

204
00:09:28,767 --> 00:09:33,821
Our home planet that needed the Star Guardians is gone. Now I strive to protect the new bonds I've forged here!

205
00:09:33,821 --> 00:09:41,668
Kuhaha! I was locked away in Trion Prison... never able to reunite with my people until the day the Land of Moa was destroyed.

206
00:09:41,668 --> 00:09:46,076
How dare you tell me to sit and endure this resentment? This anger?!

207
00:09:46,076 --> 00:09:48,453
Outrage Horn!!!

208
00:09:48,453 --> 00:09:50,740
Omega Heat Flame!!

209
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:57,856
Solid Horn... he's still as strong as ever.

210
00:09:57,856 --> 00:10:00,160
But you've gotten stronger over time too, Blue Cop!

211
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:03,265
He's distracted by Blaion's attack, so now's your chance!

212
00:10:03,265 --> 00:10:04,250
Roger that!

213
00:10:05,955 --> 00:10:07,524
Can't hold him...!!

214
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:09,669
Hang in there a little longer, Blaion!

215
00:10:09,892 --> 00:10:12,049
Alpha Bolt Cannon!!

216
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:19,835
Thunder Howl Smash!!

217
00:10:19,835 --> 00:10:22,083
Thunder Howl... Smaaash!!

218
00:10:22,083 --> 00:10:23,572
Thunder Howl... Smaa- AUGH!!

219
00:10:25,432 --> 00:10:26,682
Blue Cop!

220
00:10:28,917 --> 00:10:31,575
So you thought I was just charging in blindly.

221
00:10:31,575 --> 00:10:35,417
Wait a minute! Sniff sniff... Huh, have you already experienced the power of the beast?

222
00:10:35,417 --> 00:10:38,225
Hahahaha! It's amazing that you survived!

223
00:10:38,225 --> 00:10:42,533
No wonder you have the scent of my people. It's insulting!

224
00:10:42,533 --> 00:10:46,197
It seems your kind hasn't changed a bit over the centuries, Star Guardian.

225
00:10:46,197 --> 00:10:48,962
You still ignore your instincts and do as your master commands!

226
00:10:48,962 --> 00:10:51,985
You've been very well tamed by that little fleshling boy from this foreign land.

227
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:54,654
I didn't tame him! We're friends!!

228
00:10:54,654 --> 00:11:01,038
Hmph. As long as you’re holding the treasure of Deus Machina, there will only be those who command and those who obey.

229
00:11:01,038 --> 00:11:02,775
There are no friends for you here!

230
00:11:03,724 --> 00:11:10,806
How pitiful. To have drifted all the way to this barren wasteland, only to end up in such a sorry state because you met the wrong master!

231
00:11:10,806 --> 00:11:14,809
If I were you, I wouldn’t have let my comrades end up like this!

232
00:11:14,809 --> 00:11:17,857
I am Solid Horn, the last chieftain of the Monohorn Tribe!

233
00:11:17,857 --> 00:11:22,606
I will make this new land a place where the Wild Cardbots can live freely!

234
00:11:22,606 --> 00:11:23,240
No...! BLUE COP!!

235
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,015
Jun!!

236
00:11:24,015 --> 00:11:25,331
GROUND....

237
00:11:27,177 --> 00:11:29,840
FURY!!!!

